IMPORT prelude

-- Transport Accident Regulations 2017 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core.
--
-- Edition: S.R. No. 40/2017, Version No. 002, incorporating amendments as at 23 October 2018, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/transport-accident-regulations-2017.txt, a plain-text conversion of the Word file the
-- owner saved by hand on 2026-11-07. Line numbers below ("line 36") are lines of that text.
--
-- The Regulations only fill in what the Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) leaves to them: further severe injuries
-- (s 3(1)), the prescribed forms (ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5), 64, 86) and the greater amount for home modification
-- payments (s 60(5)). The Act has its own encoding (subjects/au/vic/transport-accident-act-1986/encodings/
-- baseline-2026-11/), but the stable l4 cannot IMPORT across subjects, so the few provisions of the Act needed here
-- are restated narrowly, each with its section and the line of the Act's deposited text (Version No. 159, as at
-- 1 November 2026, ../../../transport-accident-act-1986/registers/source-bundle/transport-accident-act-1986.txt).
--
-- BASELINE. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Transport Accident Regulations 2017 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Dates`

-- A period "after" a day does not count that day (the reading of the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Vic)
-- s 44, which is not deposited), as in the Act's encoding.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `n` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is on or before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        ((`the year` MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((`the year` MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (`the year` MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of month` `the month` `the year` MEANS
    IF `the month` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` `the year` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF `the month` EQUALS 4 OR `the month` EQUALS 6 OR `the month` EQUALS 9 OR `the month` EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The same date n months later; where that month is shorter, its last day (READING, as in the Act's encoding).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY
        (min (DATE_DAY `the day`) (`the last day of month` `the new month` `the new year`))
        `the new month`
        `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new month` MEANS (`the month index` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS (`the month index` MINUS (`the month index` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` `n` `the day` MEANS `months after` (`n` TIMES 12) `the day`

§§ `Severe injury (Act s 3(1); r 5)`

-- Act s 3(1) "severe injury, except in Part 6, means-- (a) a significant acquired brain injury, paraplegia,
-- quadriplegia, amputation of a limb, or burns to more than 50% of the body; or (b) any other injury specified by the
-- regulations for the purposes of this definition" (Act lines 212-214). Restated narrowly. The burns head is worked
-- out from the percentage of the body burned, which r 5(1)(b) also reads; the others are borrowed medical terms,
-- asked as facts.
DECLARE `Head of s 3(1)(a) other than burns` IS ONE OF
    `a significant acquired brain injury`
    `paraplegia`
    `quadriplegia`
    `amputation of a limb`
    `none of these`

-- The route by which an injury is a severe injury (the first that applies, in the order of s 3(1) and r 5(1)).
DECLARE `Severe injury route` IS ONE OF
    `s 3(1)(a) -- a brain injury, paraplegia, quadriplegia or an amputation`
    `s 3(1)(a) -- burns to more than 50% of the body`
    `r 5(1)(a) -- an injury that results in permanent blindness`
    `r 5(1)(b) -- full-thickness burns to not more than 50% of the body`
    `r 5(1)(c) -- a brachial plexus injury that results in the loss of the use of a limb`
    `not a severe injury`

-- r 5(2) (lines 42-45): "permanent blindness means-- (a) a field of vision that is constricted to 10 degrees or less
-- of arc from central fixation in the better eye, irrespective of corrected visual acuity; or (b) a corrected visual
-- acuity of less than 6/60 of the Snellen Scale in both eyes; or (c) a combination of visual defects resulting in the
-- same degree of visual loss as referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)."
-- Acuity is taken as the Snellen fraction's value (6/60 is 0.1). Whether a combination of defects gives the same
-- degree of loss is a clinical judgment: an input. The definition asks nothing about permanence (fork line 1).
GIVEN `the field of vision of the better eye in degrees` IS A NUMBER
      `the corrected visual acuity of the right eye` IS A NUMBER
      `the corrected visual acuity of the left eye` IS A NUMBER
      `a combination of visual defects gives the same degree of visual loss` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 5(2) -- is permanent blindness` `the field of vision of the better eye in degrees` `the corrected visual acuity of the right eye` `the corrected visual acuity of the left eye` `a combination of visual defects gives the same degree of visual loss` IF
        `the field of vision of the better eye in degrees` AT MOST 10
    OR  (    `the corrected visual acuity of the right eye` LESS THAN (6 DIVIDED BY 60)
         AND `the corrected visual acuity of the left eye` LESS THAN (6 DIVIDED BY 60))
    OR  `a combination of visual defects gives the same degree of visual loss`

-- r 5(1)(b) (lines 38-40): "burns to not more than 50% of the body that cause severe disfigurement and comprise of
-- full-thickness burns-- (i) to the head, neck, arms or lower legs; or (ii) that result in severe difficulties in
-- performing mobility, communication and self-care tasks". "Comprise of" is read as "include" (fork line 2);
-- "mobility, communication and self-care tasks" as all three (fork line 3). Severe disfigurement and severe
-- difficulty are clinical judgments: inputs.
GIVEN `the percentage of the body burned` IS A NUMBER
      `the burns cause severe disfigurement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are full-thickness burns to the head, neck, arms or lower legs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full-thickness burns cause severe difficulty with mobility tasks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full-thickness burns cause severe difficulty with communication tasks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full-thickness burns cause severe difficulty with self-care tasks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 5(1)(b) -- burns that are a severe injury` `the percentage of the body burned` `the burns cause severe disfigurement` `there are full-thickness burns to the head, neck, arms or lower legs` `full-thickness burns cause severe difficulty with mobility tasks` `full-thickness burns cause severe difficulty with communication tasks` `full-thickness burns cause severe difficulty with self-care tasks` IF
        `the percentage of the body burned` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the percentage of the body burned` AT MOST 50
    AND `the burns cause severe disfigurement`
    AND (   `there are full-thickness burns to the head, neck, arms or lower legs`
         OR (    `full-thickness burns cause severe difficulty with mobility tasks`
             AND `full-thickness burns cause severe difficulty with communication tasks`
             AND `full-thickness burns cause severe difficulty with self-care tasks`))

-- The facts of the injury that s 3(1) and r 5 read.
DECLARE `Injury facts` HAS
    `the other s 3(1)(a) head`                         IS A `Head of s 3(1)(a) other than burns`
    `the percentage of the body burned`                IS A NUMBER
    `severe disfigurement`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `full-thickness burns to the head, neck, arms or lower legs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `severe difficulty with mobility tasks`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `severe difficulty with communication tasks`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `severe difficulty with self-care tasks`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the field of vision of the better eye`            IS A NUMBER
    `the right eye's corrected acuity`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the left eye's corrected acuity`                  IS A NUMBER
    `a combination of defects gives the same loss`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a brachial plexus injury`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the loss of the use of a limb from it`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 3(1) with r 5(1) (lines 36-41): the route, or none. r 5(1)(c): "a brachial plexus injury that results in the loss
-- of the use of a limb". The definition is a "means" definition closed by the regulations' list, so an injury on no
-- route is not a severe injury (except in Part 6 of the Act, which the definition does not reach).
GIVEN `the injury` IS AN `Injury facts`
GIVETH A `Severe injury route`
`s 3(1), r 5 -- the severe injury route` `the injury` MEANS
    IF `another s 3(1)(a) head`
    THEN `s 3(1)(a) -- a brain injury, paraplegia, quadriplegia or an amputation`
    ELSE IF `burns to more than half`
         THEN `s 3(1)(a) -- burns to more than 50% of the body`
         ELSE IF `blindness`
              THEN `r 5(1)(a) -- an injury that results in permanent blindness`
              ELSE IF `lesser burns`
                   THEN `r 5(1)(b) -- full-thickness burns to not more than 50% of the body`
                   ELSE IF `brachial plexus`
                        THEN `r 5(1)(c) -- a brachial plexus injury that results in the loss of the use of a limb`
                        ELSE `not a severe injury`
    WHERE
        `another s 3(1)(a) head` MEANS NOT (`the injury`'s `the other s 3(1)(a) head` EQUALS `none of these`)
        `burns to more than half` MEANS `the injury`'s `the percentage of the body burned` GREATER THAN 50
        `blindness` MEANS `r 5(2) -- is permanent blindness` (`the injury`'s `the field of vision of the better eye`) (`the injury`'s `the right eye's corrected acuity`) (`the injury`'s `the left eye's corrected acuity`) (`the injury`'s `a combination of defects gives the same loss`)
        `lesser burns` MEANS `r 5(1)(b) -- burns that are a severe injury` (`the injury`'s `the percentage of the body burned`) (`the injury`'s `severe disfigurement`) (`the injury`'s `full-thickness burns to the head, neck, arms or lower legs`) (`the injury`'s `severe difficulty with mobility tasks`) (`the injury`'s `severe difficulty with communication tasks`) (`the injury`'s `severe difficulty with self-care tasks`)
        `brachial plexus` MEANS `the injury`'s `a brachial plexus injury` AND `the injury`'s `the loss of the use of a limb from it`

GIVEN `the injury` IS AN `Injury facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1), r 5 -- is a severe injury` `the injury` IF
    NOT (`s 3(1), r 5 -- the severe injury route` `the injury` EQUALS `not a severe injury`)

§§ `Home and vehicle modification payments (Act s 60(3)-(5); r 11)`

-- Act s 60(5) (Act line 2008): "The Commission must not make a payment or contribution under subsection (3) or (4)
-- which exceeds $10 000 or a greater amount as may be prescribed, unless the person enters into an agreement with
-- the Commission in relation to the ownership of, and maintenance of modifications to, the motor vehicle, home or
-- semi-detachable portable unit." s 60(3) is the motor vehicle (Act lines 1974-1976), s 60(4) the home, a
-- semi-detachable portable unit or relocation (Act lines 1989-1993). The $10 000 is not among the amounts s 61
-- varies (Act line 2092), and the prescribed amount is the Regulations', so neither is indexed.
-- r 11 (line 66): "The prescribed greater amount under section 60(5) of the Act for the purposes of section 60(4) of
-- the Act is $50 000." Nothing is prescribed for s 60(3), so a vehicle stays at $10 000.
DECLARE `Modification payment` IS ONE OF
    `a payment or contribution for the home under s 60(4)`
    `a payment or contribution for a motor vehicle under s 60(3)`

`the s 60(5) amount` MEANS 10000
`the r 11 amount` MEANS 50000

-- r 11 as now worded was substituted by S.R. No. 177/2018 reg. 3, made and in operation on 23 October 2018 (line 63
-- and the endnotes' Table of Amendments). The r 11 it replaced is not deposited. The endnotes (which are not part of
-- the Regulations) say they "will sunset ... on 6 June 2027" under s 5 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994, which
-- is not deposited. Outside 23 October 2018 to 5 June 2027 the encoding does not know the prescribed amount and
-- answers NOTHING.
`the day r 11 took its present form` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 23 10 2018
`the sunset day in the endnotes` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 6 6 2027

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 11 -- the deposited version applies on` `the day` IF
        `the day r 11 took its present form` `is on or before` `the day`
    AND NOT (`the sunset day in the endnotes` `is on or before` `the day`)

-- The most the Commission may pay or contribute, in one payment, without the agreement (fork line 4: "a payment or
-- contribution" read one at a time).
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `Modification payment`, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 60(5), r 11 -- the most without an agreement` `the payment` `the day` MEANS
    IF NOT (`r 11 -- the deposited version applies on` `the day`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the payment` EQUALS `a payment or contribution for the home under s 60(4)`
         THEN JUST `the r 11 amount`
         ELSE JUST `the s 60(5) amount`

-- Whether s 60(5) requires the agreement before this payment: yes if it "exceeds" the amount (exactly the amount
-- does not); no if it does not (fork line 5: the "unless" of s 60(5) unmet).
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `Modification payment`, `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(5), r 11 -- an agreement is needed for the payment` `the payment` `the amount` `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 60(5), r 11 -- the most without an agreement` `the payment` `the day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `the most` THEN JUST (`the amount` GREATER THAN `the most`)

§§ `The prescribed forms (rr 6-9, Schedule 1)`

DECLARE `Document` IS ONE OF
    `a statement of earnings under s 49(4), 50(4) or 51(5)`
    `a driver's report on the Commission's notice under s 64(1)`
    `a report for a recreation vehicle on the Commission's notice under s 64(3)`
    `a train or tram operator's or manager's report under s 64(2)`
    `a contract of insurance for a trailer under s 86`

DECLARE `Prescribed form` IS ONE OF
    `Form 1 -- statement of earnings by a loss of earning capacity beneficiary`
    `Form 2 -- driver's accident report`
    `Form 3 -- transport authority accident report`
    `Form 4 -- contract of insurance`

-- r 7 (line 51), r 8(1), (2) (lines 54-55), r 9 (line 58), with r 6 (Schedule 1).
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document`
GIVETH A `Prescribed form`
`rr 7-9 -- the prescribed form` `the document` MEANS
    IF `the document` EQUALS `a statement of earnings under s 49(4), 50(4) or 51(5)`
    THEN `Form 1 -- statement of earnings by a loss of earning capacity beneficiary`
    ELSE IF `a report on a notice`
         THEN `Form 2 -- driver's accident report`
         ELSE IF `the document` EQUALS `a train or tram operator's or manager's report under s 64(2)`
              THEN `Form 3 -- transport authority accident report`
              ELSE `Form 4 -- contract of insurance`
    WHERE
        `a report on a notice` MEANS
                `the document` EQUALS `a driver's report on the Commission's notice under s 64(1)`
            OR  `the document` EQUALS `a report for a recreation vehicle on the Commission's notice under s 64(3)`

-- Form 1 (lines 70-85): what the statement of earnings asks for.
`Form 1 -- the particulars asked for` MEANS
    LIST "your name, address and claim number"
         "the statement period"
         "earnings received as an employee: start date, finish date, name and address of employer, weekly hours, gross pay"
         "other earnings: start date, finish date, nature of activity, gross earnings"
         "a signed and dated declaration that the information is true and correct to the best of your knowledge and belief"

-- Act ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) (Act lines 1466, 1512, 1555), restated: a person who receives a weekly payment under the
-- section "must, within two months after each anniversary of the date on which the person first received a payment
-- under this section in respect of that accident, give the Commission a statement of earnings in the prescribed form".
-- The anniversary of 29 February in a common year is read as 28 February (READING, as in the Act's encoding).
GIVEN `the day of the first payment` IS A DATE, `the anniversary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) -- the anniversary` `the day of the first payment` `the anniversary` MEANS
    `years after` `the anniversary` `the day of the first payment`

GIVEN `the day of the first payment` IS A DATE, `the anniversary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) -- the last day for the statement of earnings` `the day of the first payment` `the anniversary` MEANS
    `months after` 2 (`ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) -- the anniversary` `the day of the first payment` `the anniversary`)

-- Given "within two months after" the anniversary: on or after the anniversary and by the last day (fork line 6: a
-- statement given before the anniversary is read as not given for that anniversary).
GIVEN `the day of the first payment` IS A DATE, `the anniversary` IS A NUMBER, `the day given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) -- the statement is given within the two months` `the day of the first payment` `the anniversary` `the day given` IF
        (`ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) -- the anniversary` `the day of the first payment` `the anniversary`) `is on or before` `the day given`
    AND `the day given` `is on or before` (`ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) -- the last day for the statement of earnings` `the day of the first payment` `the anniversary`)

§§ `Accident reports (Act s 64; r 8)`

-- Act s 64(1) (Act lines 2244-2247): "A person who is the driver of a motor vehicle, other than a recreation
-- vehicle, involved in a transport accident-- (a) as a result of which a person is or may have been injured or dies;
-- and (b) in respect of which a person may be entitled to compensation ... must, if requested by a notice served by
-- the Commission, make a report in the prescribed form within 28 days of receiving the notice". s 64(3) (Act lines
-- 2252-2259), for a recreation vehicle: "(c) if the driver of the recreation vehicle was 15 or over--is the driver;
-- or (d) if the driver of the recreation vehicle was under 15--is the owner or, if the owner was under 15, is the
-- parent or guardian of the owner". s 64(4): "Failure to comply with this section does not affect any right or
-- liability under this Act."
DECLARE `Reporter` IS ONE OF
    `the driver`
    `the owner`
    `the parent or guardian of the owner`

GIVEN `the driver's age` IS A NUMBER, `the owner's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Reporter`
`s 64(3)(c), (d) -- who reports for a recreation vehicle` `the driver's age` `the owner's age` MEANS
    IF `the driver's age` AT LEAST 15
    THEN `the driver`
    ELSE IF `the owner's age` AT LEAST 15
         THEN `the owner`
         ELSE `the parent or guardian of the owner`

GIVEN `it was a recreation vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone is or may have been injured or died and may be entitled to compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my role` IS A `Reporter`
      `the driver's age` IS A NUMBER
      `the owner's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64(1), (3) -- I am the one who must report on a notice` `it was a recreation vehicle` `someone is or may have been injured or died and may be entitled to compensation` `my role` `the driver's age` `the owner's age` IF
        `someone is or may have been injured or died and may be entitled to compensation`
    AND (IF `it was a recreation vehicle`
         THEN `my role` EQUALS (`s 64(3)(c), (d) -- who reports for a recreation vehicle` `the driver's age` `the owner's age`)
         ELSE `my role` EQUALS `the driver`)

GIVEN `the day the notice was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 64(1), (3) -- the last day for the report` `the day the notice was received` MEANS
    `days after` 28 `the day the notice was received`

§§ `The trailer contract of insurance (Act s 86; rr 9, 10; Form 4)`

-- r 10(1) (line 61): "a contract of insurance that complied, or was taken to comply, with the form prescribed by
-- regulation 10 of the Transport Accident Regulations 2007 as in force immediately before the commencement day is
-- taken to be a contract that complies with the form prescribed by regulation 9". The commencement day (r 10(2)) is
-- 6 June 2017 (endnotes).
GIVEN `the contract is in Form 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract complied with the 2007 form immediately before 6 June 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 9, r 10 -- the contract complies with the prescribed form` `the contract is in Form 4` `the contract complied with the 2007 form immediately before 6 June 2017` IF
        `the contract is in Form 4`
    OR  `the contract complied with the 2007 form immediately before 6 June 2017`

-- Form 4 cl 2 (lines 118-125): the Commission "agrees to indemnify-- (a) the owner; and (b) any other person who is at
-- any time in charge of the trailer, with or without the authority of the owner-- against any liability which may be
-- incurred ... in respect of the death of, or injury to, any person caused by, or arising out of, the use in
-- Australia of the trailer"; (2) "subject to Part 5 of the Transport Accident Act 1986; and during-- (i) the period
-- of insurance set out in the Schedule; and (ii) any subsequent period for which the Commission accepts a renewal
-- premium". cl 3(1) (lines 129-133): "This contract does not indemnify ... against any of the following-- (a)
-- liability to pay compensation under the Accident Compensation Act 1985 or an Act or law referred to in section 37
-- ...; (b) liability arising under an agreement (other than this contract) unless the liability would have arisen
-- even in the absence of the agreement; (c) liability ... in any period during which the trailer is not registered
-- in Victoria under the Interstate Road Transport Act 1985 of the Commonwealth."
-- Negatives: a case outside the grant of cl 2(1) (not the owner or a person in charge; not death or injury from use
-- in Australia) is NOTHING; outside the period of cl 2(2)(b) and under each exclusion of cl 3(1) (a flat "does not
-- indemnify") is JUST FALSE. "Subject to Part 5" is not encoded (Part 5 is s 86 itself and is left as it reads).
DECLARE `Trailer liability` HAS
    `I am the owner or a person in charge of the trailer`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the liability is for death or injury from the trailer's use in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it arose in the period of insurance or an accepted renewal`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a liability to pay workers' compensation`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `it arises only under another agreement`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trailer was registered under the Interstate Road Transport Act 1985` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the liability` IS A `Trailer liability`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Form 4 cl 2, 3(1) -- the contract indemnifies against the liability` `the liability` MEANS
    IF NOT `within the grant`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT `within the period`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `excluded`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `within the grant` MEANS
                `the liability`'s `I am the owner or a person in charge of the trailer`
            AND `the liability`'s `the liability is for death or injury from the trailer's use in Australia`
        `within the period` MEANS `the liability`'s `it arose in the period of insurance or an accepted renewal`
        `excluded` MEANS
                `the liability`'s `it is a liability to pay workers' compensation`
            OR  `the liability`'s `it arises only under another agreement`
            OR  (NOT `the liability`'s `the trailer was registered under the Interstate Road Transport Act 1985`)

-- Form 4 cl 3(2) (line 134): "If ... there subsists another contract of insurance or indemnity covering the owner in
-- respect of the same liability, the Commission is not liable under this contract for any more than its rateable
-- proportion." The contract states no way to work out the rateable proportion, so it is an input (a fraction). The
-- other contract must cover the owner; one covering only the person in charge does not trigger it (finding 6).
GIVEN `the amount of the liability` IS A NUMBER
      `another contract covers the owner for the same liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission's rateable proportion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Form 4 cl 3(2) -- the most the Commission is liable for` `the amount of the liability` `another contract covers the owner for the same liability` `the Commission's rateable proportion` MEANS
    IF `another contract covers the owner for the same liability`
    THEN `the amount of the liability` TIMES `the Commission's rateable proportion`
    ELSE `the amount of the liability`

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `TAR party` IS ONE OF
    `the person receiving weekly payments`
    `the person asked to report`

DECLARE `TAR action` IS ONE OF
    `give the statement of earnings in Form 1`
    `make the report in Form 2`

-- ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) with r 7. Clock: days from the anniversary; the days to the end of the two months are
-- worked out by the date functions and passed in.
GIVEN `the days to give the statement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TAR party` `TAR action`
`r 7 -- the statement of earnings in Form 1 within two months after each anniversary` `the days to give the statement` MEANS
    PARTY `the person receiving weekly payments`
    MUST  `give the statement of earnings in Form 1`
    WITHIN `the days to give the statement`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the person receiving weekly payments` BECAUSE "ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) with r 7: no statement of earnings in Form 1 within two months after the anniversary; at the next review no weekly payment is payable until it is given and the review is completed (Act s 55(3))"

-- s 64(1), (3) with r 8(1). Clock: days from receiving the Commission's notice.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TAR party` `TAR action`
`r 8(1) -- the report in Form 2 within 28 days of receiving the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `the person asked to report`
    MUST  `make the report in Form 2`
    WITHIN 28
    LEST  BREACH BY `the person asked to report` BECAUSE "s 64(1), (3) with r 8(1): no report in Form 2 within 28 days of receiving the notice; a $50 penalty is payable to the Commission (Act s 65(2)), and paid within 14 days after it ends no further proceedings are taken (s 66(1)(a)); no right to compensation is affected (s 64(4))"
